{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1123628-changeling-2-0-antagonists-allies","id":1123628,"title":"Changeling 2.0 Antagonists/Allies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-01T14:00:01-07:00","id":1123628,"title":"Changeling 2.0 Antagonists/Allies","content":"Eidilons, Hedge Ghosts, Hobgoblins, Hobgoblin Queens, True Fae, Fetches, Huntsmen, Loyalists/Privateers, Hedge Beasts, Fae Mounts, Ipswich Fae, Fae Touched, and possibly other things, its seems like Changeling 2.0 won't want for interesting antagonists/allies this time out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 08-04-2017, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T16:09:06-07:00","id":1123678,"title":"","content":"Our intent (and this is partly from Meghan and me, and partly our marching orders from Rich) is that the world should be alive with all sorts of weird and fascinating fae things. The antagonist section in the core is only the beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T16:45:01-07:00","id":1123700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1123628-changeling-2-0-antagonists-allies?p=1123678#post1123678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our intent (and this is partly from Meghan and me, and partly our marching orders from Rich) is that the world should be alive with all sorts of weird and fascinating fae things. The antagonist section in the core is only the beginning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much looking forward to all the new fae creatures!<br /> Will there be a mortal splat as well? like werewolf has the wolf-blooded?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T08:59:41-07:00","id":1123895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1123628-changeling-2-0-antagonists-allies?p=1123700#post1123700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very much looking forward to all the new fae creatures!<br /> Will there be a mortal splat as well? like werewolf has the wolf-blooded?</div> </div> </div> </div>The core book has fae-touched, who are people bound by a promise they made to a changeling... before that changeling was abducted. They're drawn into the Hedge and find it changing them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Appendix 1</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A woman comes home to find an uncommonly messy house. Her wife is in the kitchen, preparing dinner. Everything about the situation screams to her that something is wrong. She sees a spot of blood on the floor and as she inspects it, she sees a piece of a broken fingernail colored the same as her wife\u2019s. She looks at her wife\u2019s hand but none of the nails are broken. She makes up an excuse and leaves the house quickly, unable to return to whatever is in there. Her wife is gone, but she had promised her that she would always fight for their right to be together. The front garden is torn up, and she wonders how she didn\u2019t notice earlier. She follows the path of small details out of place until she reaches a clearing. She sees two paths that look exactly the same, but her heart points her left and she does not hesitate before stepping off in that direction.</div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T09:24:07-07:00","id":1123901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1123628-changeling-2-0-antagonists-allies?p=1123895#post1123895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The core book has fae-touched, who are people bound by a promise they made to a changeling... before that changeling was abducted. They're drawn into the Hedge and find it changing them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Largely unchanged (from the previews), then? Probably interact with the Common/Royal divide, if they use Contracts at all.<br /> <br /> Is there any space or anything planned for those descended from fae (Changeling, Goblin, or other)? Those born in Arcadia or the Hedge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T09:42:56-07:00","id":1123907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1123628-changeling-2-0-antagonists-allies?p=1123901#post1123901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any space or anything planned for those descended from fae (Changeling, Goblin, or other)? Those born in Arcadia or the Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be a post-core thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T09:55:32-07:00","id":1123910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1123628-changeling-2-0-antagonists-allies?p=1123907#post1123907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That'd be a post-core thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heirs to Hell equivalents for other lines would be a treat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T10:09:22-07:00","id":1123914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1123628-changeling-2-0-antagonists-allies?p=1123907#post1123907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That'd be a post-core thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. So don't post the ideas I have on it (for worry that it creates some tangled IP mess)? I mean, in the unlikely event it is even close to what is planned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T10:14:52-07:00","id":1123917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1123628-changeling-2-0-antagonists-allies?p=1123910#post1123910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heirs to Hell equivalents for other lines would be a treat.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was this weird old bias in White Wolf stuff (and to be fair, I've been part of it) to portray parenthood as just completely off-limits to supernatural creatures.* I noticed this less when I was younger, because hey, we were all wild and free and knew about birth control, right? (And not to put too fine a point on it, but when I was growing up, the idea that us queer people would never have kids was kind of pervasive.)<br /> <br /> But I'm in my mid-thirties now, and although I'm child-free, plenty of my friends are parents. Some of them are even parents of adults. And so it's started to seem weird that a setting that dwells so much on the everyday struggles and value of being a person walls off that range of experience.<br /> <br /> It's one thing to say, well, part of the tragedy of being a vampire is that you can never have kids again, or that being cut off from the family you began is one of the pains of returning from Arcadia. Those are plot points, those are conflicts. But I look around, and I see kids picking things up from their parents, parents trying to pass things onto their kids, the strains and fears** that come with having that kind of a family, and it seems very artificial that we never cover that in our otherwise deep dives into relationships and subcultures.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to call portraying parenthood (or childhood) a major new agenda of the Chronicles of Darkness, but over the last few years I've been trying to make sure that we consider it in our exploration of human experience. I pitched <i>Heirs to Hell </i>specifically for that reason, and you'll see more of it in the future<i>.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Or to do pregnancy horror. I guess we did a fair bit of that, and not much of it written by people who'd been pregnant.<br /> ** Nope, I haven't forgotten it's a horror game.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 08-02-2017, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T10:39:34-07:00","id":1123923,"title":"","content":"I must say, that one of my secret desperate hopes is that someday, we would get a guide to play Fetches as protagonists. I can't exactly say why, but I have always felt sympathy toward them- waking up one day and discovering that you live life which aren't yours, and that someone else who looks exactly like you decides to come and kill you because you stole them from him, someone you feel strangely connected with. You know that he is right, and that you are nothing but a wisp of shadow and few fallen leaves someone found on the ground- but those are your life. You may be made out of lies, but you are real- and you should protect the life you stole even at the cost of killing your true self, because you deserve it more than that old you- like the Shadow from Hans Christian Anderson's story.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it is definitely not something for a core book, but I do hope that maybe we'll get it in a future supplement (even if the chances aren't that high)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 08-02-2017, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T10:41:59-07:00","id":1123924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1123628-changeling-2-0-antagonists-allies?p=1123923#post1123923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say, that one of my secret desperate hopes is that someday, we would get a guide to play Fetches as protagonists. I can't exactly say way, but I have always felt sympathy toward them- waking up one day and discovering that you live life which aren't yours, and that someone else who looks exactly like you decides to come and kill you because you stole them from him, someone you feel strangely connected with. You know that he is right, and that you are nothing but a wisp of shadow and few fallen leaves someone found on the ground- but those are your life. You may be made out of lies, but you are real- and you should protect the life you stole even at the cost of killing your true self, because you deserve it more than that old you- like the Shadow from Hans Christian Anderson's story.<br /> <br /> Yeah, it is definitely not something for a core book, but I do hope that maybe we'll get it in a future supplement (even if the chances aren't that high)</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to see this as well! I've always thought that things from the perspective of the Fetch would be super interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T10:45:43-07:00","id":1123926,"title":"","content":"Here's a thing that I was very blunt with the writers about on 2e: Fetches are people. Changelings might not see them that way, and they may be quite sinister people. But they're definitely people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T12:10:13-07:00","id":1123965,"title":"","content":"To expand on that: figuratively, having a Fetch is about being replaced. Your Fetch is your ex's new boyfriend... who might be just <i>so</i> perfect you want to puke or might be completely <i>awful</i> and how the hell can he have left you for <i>that</i>? Your Fetch is your mom's surrogate son... God, it's a hell of a thing to find out that what she really wanted was an office drone who votes Democrat but complains constantly about SJWs, isn't it? In order for that figurative layer to work, two things have to be true:<br /> <br /> 1) Your Fetch has to be a real person.<br /> <br /> 2) Your Fetch can't be you.<br /> <br /> But this is the Chronicles of Darkness. We do cool things on figurative levels, but we're not in the business of allegory. So your Fetch is <i>also</i> a stuffed doll who sews his eyes back on every morning when he thinks he's putting on his glasses. She <i>also</i> quit your soccer team because instead of your lanky arms she has limbs that are literally sharpened sticks.<br /> <br /> And somehow, everybody has to live in a world where these things are true. Unless some people need to stop living. (God, how did you become the person that can even think that?)<br /> <br /> Well... maybe you could share? Joint custody of a life. Like a twin swap in <i>Sweet Valley High</i>. (Because those always worked out so well, right?)<br /> <br /> Or there was that one time you saw a magician in a goblin market turn two goats into one. Can that be done with people? Would that be okay? (What if neither of you ended up being you?)<br /> <br /> No easy answers, I'm afraid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 08-02-2017, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T12:11:36-07:00","id":1123966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1123628-changeling-2-0-antagonists-allies?p=1123917#post1123917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There was this weird old bias in White Wolf stuff (and to be fair, I've been part of it) to portray parenthood as just completely off-limits to supernatural creatures.* I noticed this less when I was younger, because hey, we were all wild and free and knew about birth control, right? (And not to put too fine a point on it, but when I was growing up, the idea that us queer people would never have kids was kind of pervasive.)<br /> <br /> But I'm in my mid-thirties now, and although I'm child-free, plenty of my friends are parents. Some of them are even parents of adults. And so it's started to seem weird that a setting that dwells so much on the everyday struggles and value of being a person walls off that range of experience.<br /> <br /> It's one thing to say, well, part of the tragedy of being a vampire is that you can never have kids again, or that being cut off from the family you began is one of the pains of returning from Arcadia. Those are plot points, those are conflicts. But I look around, and I see kids picking things up from their parents, parents trying to pass things onto their kids, the strains and fears** that come with having that kind of a family, and it seems very artificial that we never cover that in our otherwise deep dives into relationships and subcultures.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to call portraying parenthood (or childhood) a major new agenda of the Chronicles of Darkness, but over the last few years I've been trying to make sure that we consider it in our exploration of human experience. I pitched <i>Heirs to Hell </i>specifically for that reason, and you'll see more of it in the future<i>.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Or to do pregnancy horror. I guess we did a fair bit of that, and not much of it written by people who'd been pregnant.<br /> ** Nope, I haven't forgotten it's a horror game.</span></div> </div> </div> </div> It clearly ties into Half Damned and even Secrets of the Covenants which basically sets things up for Half Damned and offers an alternative sort of way of becoming a parent with via giving birth to a Cruac God.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T12:30:57-07:00","id":1123971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1123628-changeling-2-0-antagonists-allies?p=1123966#post1123966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It clearly ties into Half Damned and even Secrets of the Covenants which basically sets things up for Half Damned and offers an alternative sort of way of becoming a parent with via giving birth to a Cruac God.</div> </div> </div> </div>Danielle and I sat down at Gen Con last year and had a long talk about <i>Half-Damned</i>. We'd looked at dhampir in <i>Wicked Dead</i>, and we loved the conflicts they set up for vampires. But when you're looking at player characters (or even just a part of the mythos that we mention more than once), being a literal curse seemed too one-note. And Danielle's insight was that if you have dhampir in the first place, and you have Kindred trying to be parents (or abandoning their kids) when the Requiem is usually one long solo... well, you've got plenty of conflict right there.<br /> <br /> So you'll see in <i>Half-Damned</i> that although there are definitely some unique supernatural angles, and while the conflicts from <i>Wicked Dead</i> are still there, the <i>Vampire </i>team looked at them much more from the perspective of &quot;okay, what would actually happen if occasionally a vampire becomes a mom? what are all the ways that could go wrong? and most importantly: why would they do it anyway?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T12:33:23-07:00","id":1123973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1123628-changeling-2-0-antagonists-allies?p=1123917#post1123917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was this weird old bias in White Wolf stuff (and to be fair, I've been part of it) to portray parenthood as just completely off-limits to supernatural creatures.*</div> </div> </div> </div>That! That explains Cleave to the Herd and unihar. And changelings being sterile in first edition. It's like Spider-man and Superman being married.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not going to call portraying parenthood (or childhood) a major new agenda of the Chronicles of Darkness, but over the last few years I've been trying to make sure that we consider it in our exploration of human experience. I pitched <i>Heirs to Hell </i>specifically for that reason, and you'll see more of it in the future<i>.</i> </div> </div> </div>As a 30 something with a kid it's actually something I've been wanting for a while. Before the kid and all I just thought it would be interesting to deal with a kid in a character's life, even if they were away in college it's still a concern not to, like, enrage the kind of enemies who would wipe your lineage from the face of the Earth or ensure that the college isn't a breeding ground for monsters. Not necessarily to make it the forefront part of a story or anything, but for characters sometimes there's more at risk when you've been Embraced and have a family to deal with rather than being an heiress with no personal connections to anyone. And inner conflict in a werewolf torn between a desire to keep their familial 'pack' safe and cut them off due to the increasing danger of their new lifestyle. And hunter was always supposed to be normal people thrust into something else and deciding to do something about it, but seemed prone to more Punisher-esque hate machines directed at the supernatural.<br /> <br /> It's not for everyone, though, that kind of choice in character, most of my player characters are considerably younger and would balk at parenthood. The wolf-blooded seemed to have been handled well. But everyone having magic kids seems like it would be too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-02-2017, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T14:49:43-07:00","id":1124015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1123628-changeling-2-0-antagonists-allies?p=1123973#post1123973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like Spider-man and Superman being married.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is.<br /> <br /> If I were being really cynical, I might keep doing it for the same reasons Spider-Man and Superman got reset. Cling to the idea that what the Darkness games are selling is an idealized young adulthood. That even though they're scary places (with plenty of serious stuff like guns and blood), ultimately they're about people who never have a hair out of place (except when attractively mussed), always fit into the first pair of jeans they try on (which are leather), and do it with all the sexiest people (who don't need anything afterward).<br /> <br /> But that's not worldbuilding, it's porn.<br /> <br /> Taking an incredibly narrow section of life experience (that nobody ever <i>quite</i> had) and putting it in glossy packaging is leaving out the incredible variety of human life, both good and bad. Naturally, each of our games focus on a subset of life experiences, but, like, what the hell are we doing in <i>Changeling</i> if we can't look at why you <i>want</i> your life back? How honest is a game about the beautiful and mad act of claiming your own life if the only lives we show are As Seen On TV?<br /> <br /> I mean, that's not being a changeling, that's being True Fae.<br /> <br /> Sure, games are dramas and they should be thrilling and spectacular and they should give you experiences reality never does... but they should be honest. And this game, especially, should be honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 08-02-2017, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T21:58:00-07:00","id":1124176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1123628-changeling-2-0-antagonists-allies?p=1124015#post1124015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is.<br /> <br /> If I were being really cynical, I might keep doing it for the same reasons Spider-Man and Superman got reset. Cling to the idea that what the Darkness games are selling is an idealized young adulthood. That even though they're scary places (with plenty of serious stuff like guns and blood), ultimately they're about people who never have a hair out of place (except when attractively mussed), always fit into the first pair of jeans they try on (which are leather), and do it with all the sexiest people (who don't need anything afterward).<br /> <br /> But that's not worldbuilding, it's porn.<br /> <br /> Taking an incredibly narrow section of life experience (that nobody ever <i>quite</i> had) and putting it in glossy packaging is leaving out the incredible variety of human life, both good and bad. Naturally, each of our games focus on a subset of life experiences, but, like, what the hell are we doing in <i>Changeling</i> if we can't look at why you <i>want</i> your life back? How honest is a game about the beautiful and mad act of claiming your own life if the only lives we show are As Seen On TV?<br /> <br /> I mean, that's not being a changeling, that's being True Fae.<br /> <br /> Sure, games are dramas and they should be thrilling and spectacular and they should give you experiences reality never does... but they should be honest. And this game, especially, should be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only like, love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T00:36:06-07:00","id":1124208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1123628-changeling-2-0-antagonists-allies?p=1123965#post1123965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) Your Fetch has to be a real person.<br /> <br /> 2) Your Fetch can't be you.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly enough, a 2e Changeling I've been refining for quite a while plays with the idea of the Changeling outright protecting his Fetch for a simple reason: his Keeper robbed him of most if not all his memories, so while his Fetch may not exactly be as he was, his Fetch is still the last remnant of his original self. If his Fetch dies, the person he was is all but gone for good. He really won't stand for that to happen. Problem is, his mien isn't really that human (closer to a costume than anything else), so approaching his Fetch may not be easy.<br /> <br /> Ideally the two parts would be put back together again, or at least the pair would become amiable, but the Chronicles of Darkness is rarely so kind, so it'd remain to be seen what would happen in a campaign with them.<br /> <br /> Still, really awesome that Fetches are being given more of an established dilemna to them rather than being treated as mere tools of a Keeper. It was present in 1e, but still.<br /> <br /> Also, when the example of &quot;when Superman and Spiderman married&quot;, it took me a moment to realize that the discussion was about their respective marriages, and not some weird crossover comic where the two married one another (though I don't doubt some fanfic somewhere has made that happen).<br /> <br /> And on the subject of a player character being a parent, I'm all for that being more of an established thing. In Demon I'm looking forward t having my character using pacts to either adopt a child from a family who would not be good for said child, or for relieving someone of an unwanted pregnancy. I like the idea of having a story involving taking care of a child, raising them in this dark and terrifying world...which is kind of weird, given I'm a gay man in real life with no real desire for kids. I'd love to see what Changeling could offer in that regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 08-03-2017, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T04:25:47-07:00","id":1124691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1123628-changeling-2-0-antagonists-allies?p=1123895#post1123895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core book has fae-touched, who are people bound by a promise they made to a changeling... before that changeling was abducted. They're drawn into the Hedge and find it changing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1123628-changeling-2-0-antagonists-allies?p=1123923#post1123923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say, that one of my secret desperate hopes is that someday, we would get a guide to play Fetches as protagonists. I can't exactly say why, but I have always felt sympathy toward them- waking up one day and discovering that you live life which aren't yours, and that someone else who looks exactly like you decides to come and kill you because you stole them from him, someone you feel strangely connected with. You know that he is right, and that you are nothing but a wisp of shadow and few fallen leaves someone found on the ground- but those are your life. You may be made out of lies, but you are real- and you should protect the life you stole even at the cost of killing your true self, because you deserve it more than that old you- like the Shadow from Hans Christian Anderson's story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like fetches too. I always like the options where they and the changeling make peace (I had a character whose fetch was instrumental in her successfully making it through the hedge).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T14:04:35-07:00","id":1124935,"title":"","content":"I forgot Fae Mounts, the Ipswich Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}